{"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}],"role":"collection","roleHeading":"Framework","title":"Traffluent","externalID":"Traffluent","symbolKind":"module"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Typed analytics events for Swift, delivered in batches to any number of destinations."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChoosingDestinations","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingFromViews","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TestingWhatYouTrack"],"anchor":"Essentials","title":"Essentials"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SessionsAndStandardContext","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SamplingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/DefiningEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WritingAVendorDestination"],"anchor":"Guides","title":"Guides"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WhatGoesWhere","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChangingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/IdentifyingPeople","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PrivacyManifests"],"anchor":"Choosing-what-to-record","title":"Choosing what to record"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events","doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers","doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking","doc:\/\/UIKitTracking\/documentation\/UIKitTracking","doc:\/\/AppKitTracking\/documentation\/AppKitTracking","doc:\/\/AutomaticScreenTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticScreenTracking","doc:\/\/AutomaticControlTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticControlTracking","doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking","doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions","doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations","doc:\/\/LoggingDestinations\/documentation\/LoggingDestinations","doc:\/\/TracingDestinations\/documentation\/TracingDestinations","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding","doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding","doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding","doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding","doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding","doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding","doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding","doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding","doc:\/\/HeapEncoding\/documentation\/HeapEncoding","doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding","doc:\/\/PropertyJSON\/documentation\/PropertyJSON","doc:\/\/JSONValues\/documentation\/JSONValues","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence","doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans","doc:\/\/AsyncQueues\/documentation\/AsyncQueues","doc:\/\/Checksums\/documentation\/Checksums"],"anchor":"Modules","title":"Modules"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting","doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting","doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting"],"anchor":"Testing","title":"Testing"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each event is a struct, so the compiler checks its name and every property. A tracker holds back"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the events the user hasn’t consented to, stamps the rest with their session and device, keeps them"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on disk and delivers them to your server, sending again when the network or the server fails."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"An app’s analytics, from launch","anchor":"An-apps-analytics-from-launch"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare the events. The tracker rejects an event that breaks a constraint before it is stored or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivered, and a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" value reaches only the destinations that don’t redact it:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import SwiftUI","import Traffluent","import TrackingPlans","","@Event(name: \"product_added_to_cart\")","struct ProductAddedToCart {","    var productID: String","    @Constrained(.minimum(1), .maximum(10))","    var quantity: Int","}","","@Event(name: \"signed_up\")","struct SignedUp {","    var plan: String","    var email: Sensitive<String>","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Build the tracker and start its delivery once, as the app launches:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["func startAnalytics(consent: Consent) throws -> Tracker {","    \/\/ The plan and the store each take every @Event in the app, and the library's own.","    let plan = try TrackingPlan()","    \/\/ Records wait on disk until they are delivered, across launches.","    let store = try SegmentStore()","    \/\/ Every event gets its session, and the app, device, OS, locale and network it was tracked on.","    let tracker = Tracker(","        store: store,","        consent: consent,","        enrichers: [.sessions(), .application(), .device(), .operatingSystem(), .locale(), .network()])","","    let collector = HTTPDestination(","        endpoint: collectorURL,","        headerFields: [.authorization: \"Bearer \\(apiKey)\"],","        encoder: CollectorBatchEncoder(plan: plan))","    \/\/ Analytics events only, without their email addresses, 20 at a time or every 30 seconds.","    let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(","        to: collector.accepting(.analytics).redactingSensitiveValues())","    Task {","        do {","            try await delivery.execute()  \/\/ for the life of the app","        } catch {","            print(\"Delivery stopped: \\(error)\")","        }","    }","","    \/\/ Every event that won't arrive, and why.","    let rejections = tracker.rejectionReports","    let consentDrops = consent.dropReports","    let storeDrops = store.dropReports","    let collectorDrops = collector.dropReports","    Task {","        await withDiscardingTaskGroup { group in","            group.addTask { for await report in rejections { print(\"Rejected: \\(report)\") } }","            group.addTask { for await report in consentDrops { print(\"Not consented: \\(report)\") } }","            group.addTask { for await report in storeDrops { print(\"Not stored: \\(report)\") } }","            group.addTask { for await report in collectorDrops { print(\"Not sent: \\(report)\") } }","        }","    }","    return tracker","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Then make the tracker the app’s default and hand it to the views, which track through it:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["@main","struct StoreApp: App {","    let tracker: Tracker","","    init() {","        do {","            \/\/ The user's earlier decisions, which the app saved; undecided categories wait in memory.","            let tracker = try startAnalytics(consent: Consent(savedDecisions))","            \/\/ `Tracker.current` falls back to it where nothing else reaches, such as a detached task.","            try Tracker.bootstrap(tracker)","            self.tracker = tracker","        } catch {","            print(\"Analytics are off: \\(error)\")","            tracker = .noOp","        }","    }","","    var body: some Scene {","        WindowGroup {","            CartView()","                .tracker(tracker)","        }","    }","}","","struct CartView: View {","    @Environment(\\.tracker) private var tracker","","    var body: some View {","        Button(\"Add to Cart\") {","            tracker.track(ProductAddedToCart(productID: \"canvas-tote\", quantity: 1))","        }","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" imports every module except ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeapEncoding\/documentation\/HeapEncoding","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/PropertyJSON\/documentation\/PropertyJSON","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/JSONValues\/documentation\/JSONValues","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and the testing modules, which are products of their own.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Where to go next","anchor":"Where-to-go-next"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Set it up step by step, from adding the package to testing what you track: "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/GettingStarted"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Declare events and their constraints: ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/DefiningEvents","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"; change one that has shipped:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChangingEvents","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Track from SwiftUI, UIKit and AppKit views: ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingFromViews","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"; let screens, controls and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the app’s lifecycle track themselves: ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reach the tracker from any code, batch records and add context to them: "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingEvents","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep events when the app ends or goes offline before delivering them: "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Ask for consent and gate events by it: "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep a fraction of events or sessions: "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SamplingEvents"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Group events into sessions and stamp them with the app and device: ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SessionsAndStandardContext"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A session’s key is a UUIDv7, its start time in Unix milliseconds followed by random bits, held in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"memory only.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Export the events’ schemas and catch breaking changes in CI: "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Test what your code tracks: "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TestingWhatYouTrack"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Send to logs, traces, your own server, PostHog, Amplitude, Mixpanel, Segment, RudderStack,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Customer.io, Google Analytics from a server or memory, with values for one destination alone:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChoosingDestinations","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Send to an analytics vendor not yet covered, from a module of your own:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WritingAVendorDestination"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Decide what belongs in an event and what stays out of it: "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WhatGoesWhere","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/IdentifyingPeople","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PrivacyManifests","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/traffluent"]}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/ConsentGating":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/consentgating","role":"article","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating","type":"topic","title":"Consent Gating","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Deliver an event only once the user grants the purpose it is collected for."}]},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/AutomaticTracking":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/automatictracking","role":"article","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking","type":"topic","title":"Automatic Tracking","abstract":[{"text":"Track screen views, control activations and the app’s lifecycle without a call at each place they happen.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/IdentifyingPeople":{"kind":"article","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Traffluent knows people only by a pseudonymous session. An identifier that outlives one is yours to add, store, reset and gate with consent.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/IdentifyingPeople","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/identifyingpeople","type":"topic","title":"Identifying People"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TrackingEvents":{"kind":"article","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Track typed events with a tracker, then deliver them in batches to any number of destinations."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingEvents","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingevents","type":"topic","title":"Tracking Events"},"doc://Trackers/documentation/Trackers":{"url":"\/documentation\/trackers","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers","type":"topic","title":"Trackers","abstract":[{"text":"The tracker app code tracks events with, and what it applies to each event before it is delivered: enrichers, samplers and consent.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Events/documentation/Events":{"url":"\/documentation\/events","title":"Events","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The types every other module shares: the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event"},{"text":" protocol, the values its properties can hold, and the record a tracker makes of each event.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/SamplingEvents":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/samplingevents","role":"article","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SamplingEvents","type":"topic","title":"Sampling Events","abstract":[{"text":"Keep a seeded fraction of the events a tracker tracks, event by event or a whole session at once.","type":"text"}]},"doc://AppKitTracking/documentation/AppKitTracking":{"url":"\/documentation\/appkittracking","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AppKitTracking\/documentation\/AppKitTracking","type":"topic","title":"AppKitTracking","abstract":[{"text":"Let AppKit views find their tracker up the responder chain, and track what controls do.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/WritingAVendorDestination":{"kind":"article","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Send events to an analytics vendor Traffluent doesn’t cover yet, from a module of your own, with the same rules as the destinations it ships.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WritingAVendorDestination","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/writingavendordestination","type":"topic","title":"Writing a Vendor Destination"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/WhatGoesWhere":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/whatgoeswhere","title":"Logging, Tracing, Metrics and Analytics","role":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WhatGoesWhere","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Four signals, four jobs. Decide which one a fact belongs to before you write the line that records it."}]},"doc://PostHogEncoding/documentation/PostHogEncoding":{"url":"\/documentation\/posthogencoding","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding","type":"topic","title":"PostHogEncoding","abstract":[{"text":"Send records to PostHog Cloud or a self-hosted PostHog through its batch capture API.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/ChangingEvents":{"kind":"article","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"An event’s version counts the changes that records stored before them can’t be read through, and only those. A compatible change keeps the version; a breaking one raises it.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChangingEvents","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/changingevents","type":"topic","title":"Changing an Event"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TrackingPlanWorkflow":{"kind":"article","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Tell the people and services that read your events what each event holds, and hear about a change that would break their data before it ships."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingplanworkflow","type":"topic","title":"Exporting and Checking a Tracking Plan"},"doc://TracingDestinations/documentation/TracingDestinations":{"url":"\/documentation\/tracingdestinations","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/TracingDestinations\/documentation\/TracingDestinations","type":"topic","title":"TracingDestinations","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A destination that adds each tracked event to the span that was active when it was tracked."}]},"doc://PropertyJSON/documentation/PropertyJSON":{"url":"\/documentation\/propertyjson","title":"PropertyJSON","role":"collection","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/PropertyJSON\/documentation\/PropertyJSON","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The vendor-neutral pieces a JSON "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" is built from: properties, context, timestamps, identity and batch splitting."}]},"doc://SegmentSpecEncoding/documentation/SegmentSpecEncoding":{"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records as Segment-spec track calls to Segment, RudderStack or Customer.io Data Pipelines."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding","url":"\/documentation\/segmentspecencoding","type":"topic","title":"SegmentSpecEncoding"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations":{"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","type":"topic","title":"HTTPDestinations","abstract":[{"text":"Send each batch of records to an HTTP endpoint, and send it again until it arrives.","type":"text"}]},"doc://AptabaseEncoding/documentation/AptabaseEncoding":{"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to Aptabase, in its cloud or on your own server, through its events API."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding","url":"\/documentation\/aptabaseencoding","type":"topic","title":"AptabaseEncoding"},"doc://Checksums/documentation/Checksums":{"url":"\/documentation\/checksums","title":"Checksums","role":"collection","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Checksums\/documentation\/Checksums","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The CRC-32 checksum of raw bytes, as zlib, PNG, gzip and Ethernet compute it.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Destinations/documentation/Destinations":{"url":"\/documentation\/destinations","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations","type":"topic","title":"Destinations","abstract":[{"text":"Where tracked events go: the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Destination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" protocol, the modifiers that narrow what a destination receives, and the delivery that hands it batches.","type":"text"}]},"doc://MatomoEncoding/documentation/MatomoEncoding":{"url":"\/documentation\/matomoencoding","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding","type":"topic","title":"MatomoEncoding","abstract":[{"text":"Send records to a Matomo installation as events, through its bulk tracking API.","type":"text"}]},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding":{"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","abstract":[{"text":"Send records to a Mixpanel project through its track API.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding","url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding","type":"topic","title":"MixpanelEncoding"},"doc://DestinationTesting/documentation/DestinationTesting":{"url":"\/documentation\/destinationtesting","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting","type":"topic","title":"DestinationTesting","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Check from Swift Testing that a vendor destination keeps the library’s rules and sends what its fixtures record."}]},"doc://SnowplowEncoding/documentation/SnowplowEncoding":{"url":"\/documentation\/snowplowencoding","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding","type":"topic","title":"SnowplowEncoding","abstract":[{"text":"Send records to a Snowplow collector as self-describing events, whose schemas come from the tracking plan.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/DefiningEvents":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/de